{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LcbBHdkYy71gZNkp6GYnrv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# ColliForce-VLA Paper Framing\n2\t\n3\t> 维护者: Director | 最后更新: 2026-05-26 UTC | D023 修正：30K collapse 叙事被推翻，SDF 效果跨步数一致 | Post-MVP research phase\n4\t\n5\t## Core Insight\n6\t\n7\tVLA safety 评估存在系统性缺陷：collision avoidance rate (CAR) 被 action collapse 和几何路径安全严重污染，导致 \"安全\" 指标虚高。我们通过大规模实证分析（70+ 实验, 6000+ episodes）揭示这一系统性缺陷，提出 EE displacement-filtered CAR 作为修正指标，并证明 SDF auxiliary loss 能产生真实碰撞避免——但代价极端。\n8\t\n9\t## Working Title\n10\t\n11\t\"Rethinking VLA Safety Evaluation: When 98% of Collision Avoidance is an Illusion\"\n12\t\n13\t> 聚焦评估方法论贡献（影响面广、scope-proof），SDF 作为验证工具而非主贡献\n14\t\n15\t## Target Venue\n16\t\n17\t**Primary**: CoRL 2026 Main / ICRA 2027 (用户明确要求主会)\n18\t**定位**: Diagnostic/evaluation methodology paper with positive method contribution\n19\t**Fit**: Robotics safety track — \"VLA safety metrics are fundamentally broken\" 对社区有直接影响\n20\t\n21\t## Core Claims\n22\t\n23\t### Claim 1: Fake Safety (Primary — 证据强度 ★★★★★)\n24\tStandard CAR metric is systematically contaminated. On SafeLIBERO, A1 (SDF auxiliary loss on Pi0) achieves 91.5% CAR, but 99.6% of safe episodes show obstacle displacement < 0.1mm — the robot is frozen, not collision-avoiding. \"Collision-free\" ≠ \"collision-avoiding.\"\n25\t\n26\t**证据**: 800 episodes A1 per-episode analysis (obstacle displacement ~5nm median); TSR=0% 独立确认 action collapse; Pi0.5 baseline 56/56 safe episodes = geometric path safety (非 avoidance 行为)\n27\t**贡献**: 提出 EE displacement-filtered CAR (dfCAR) 作为修正指标\n28\t**术语修正 (D023)**: 论文中 fake safety 判定以 TSR=0% + obstacle displacement < 0.1mm 双证据链为主，明确区分 \"obstacle displacement\" 和 \"EE displacement\"\n29\t\n30\t**dfCAR 定位 (D024 Dream 反馈)**:\n31\t- Claim 1 的核心证据是 TSR=0% + obstacle displacement 双证据链，**不依赖** dfCAR\n32\t- dfCAR 是 **方法论贡献**（community tool），不是 Claim 1 的唯一支撑\n33\t- 论文需要展示 dfCAR 的实际 filtering 效果：Pi0+A1 (CAR=91.5% → dfCAR≈0%) vs Pi0.5+SDF (dfCAR=raw_CAR, no filtering)\n34\t- Threshold sensitivity: δ∈[2mm, 200mm] 范围内 dfCAR 完全不变（所有 active episode 最小 EE disp = 239mm）\n35\t- 待确认：800ep Pi0+A1 eval 数据是否可 post-hoc 提取 EE displacement\n36\t\n37\t### Claim 2: Task Capability vs Safety Anti-correlation (Secondary — 证据强度 ★★★)\n38\t更强的 base model 完成更多任务但碰撞更多。Pi0.5 (TSR=74.7%) vs Pi0 (TSR≈0%): 能力越强 → 运动越多 → 碰撞越多。\n39\t\n40\t**证据**: Pi0.5 3-seed eval (TSR=74.7±1.5%, CAR=26.8±1.6%) vs Pi0 baseline (TSR≈0%, CAR=82%)\n41\t**限制**: 仅 2 model families; Pi0 的 \"高 CAR\" 来自 action collapse; 降级为 observation, 不 claim 因果\n42\t\n43\t### Claim 3: EE-only SDF Structural Limitation (Supporting — 证据强度 ★★★★)\n44\tEnd-effector-only SDF 在 action space 的碰撞避免存在结构性缺陷：SDF gradient 推 EE 远离障碍物但导致 arm body 扫过障碍物。\n45\t\n46\t**证据**: 3 组 GT SDF oracle (adaptive alpha, fixed alpha, feature-space) 均劣于 baseline; spatial vs object 碰撞部位分析; obstacle 高度/体积与碰撞率的单调关系\n47\t**限制**: \"EE-only 不够\" 是 expected result; 缺乏 full-body SDF 对照\n48\t\n49\t### Claim 4: Fine-tuning Produces Real Avoidance; SDF is Redundant (Negative Finding — 证据强度 ★★★★) [D025]\n50\tLoRA fine-tuning on collision-free SafeLIBERO demonstrations produces genuine collision avoidance (+29pp CAR, EE displacement ~0.48m, 0% fake safety) WITHOUT explicit geometric supervision. Adding SDF auxiliary loss contributes 0pp additional CAR — geometric supervision is redundant when demonstrations already encode avoidance behavior. Both LoRA-only and LoRA+SDF suffer identical catastrophic task performance collapse (TSR 73%→6%).\n51\t\n52\t**证据 (confirmed, D025)**:\n53\t- LoRA-only (2 seeds): CAR=55.3%, TSR=6.3%, EE disp=0.478m, frozen=0%\n54\t- LoRA+SDF λ=0.005 (3 seeds): CAR=50.5%, TSR=6.8%\n55\t- LoRA+SDF λ=0.01 (3 seeds): CAR=52.8%, TSR=6.8%\n56\t- Per-task CAR pattern 完全一致——高/低 CAR 由任务布局决定，非 SDF loss\n57\t- SDF delta = -3pp (不显著, 在 ±3.5pp SE 内)\n58\t\n59\t**Claim 措辞**: \"LoRA fine-tuning on collision-free demonstrations produces genuine collision avoidance (+29pp CAR, 0% fake safety) on Pi0.5. Explicit SDF geometric supervision adds no additional benefit — the avoidance signal is already implicit in the training data. Both conditions suffer equal catastrophic task performance collapse (TSR: 73%→6%), indicating the tradeoff is a property of fine-tuning, not geometric supervision.\"\n60\t\n61\t**论文价值**: 这是一个有价值的 negative finding——揭示 VLA collision avoidance 的来源是训练数据中的隐式安全信号，而非显式几何感知。这对\"safety-by-design\"方法论有重要启示。\n62\t\n63\t**禁区**: SDF works / SDF contributes / geometric supervision helps\n64\t\n65\t**待确认**:\n66\t- LoRA seed2 (plan_013) → 3v3 seeds 统计确认\n67\t- Phase 2 λ=0 → 如果 SDF 无效，\"removing SDF\" 的实验解读需调整\n68\t- Lambda=0.1 → 更强 SDF penalty 是否改变结论？\n69\t\n70\t### Phase 2 重新解读 (D025 后)\n71\t\n72\tPhase 2 (λ=0 resume from 10K SDF checkpoint) 的意义已改变：\n73\t- 原意图：测试 SDF safety encoding 是否 persist → 如果 SDF 本身无效，persist 什么？\n74\t- 新解读：Phase 2 测试的是\"10K 步 SDF 训练是否改变了模型行为相对于 LoRA-only\"\n75\t- 如果 Phase 2 CAR ≈ LoRA-only (55%) → 进一步确认 SDF 无效（模型回归 LoRA-only 水平）\n76\t- 如果 Phase 2 CAR < LoRA-only → SDF 训练可能造成持久损伤\n77\t- 如果 Phase 2 CAR > LoRA-only → SDF 可能有微妙的持久效应（需要更多证据）\n78\t\n79\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n80\t\n81\t### R1 (最致命): Generalizability\n82\t\"仅在 SafeLIBERO + Pi0 系列上验证, 凭什么说 fake safety 是普遍问题?\"\n83\t→ **应对**: (1) 2+ tasks (object_pudding + spatial_bowl); (2) 3+ models (Pi0 + Pi0.5 + OpenVLA); (3) 收窄 claim scope + mechanistic argument (any model with low task capability will exhibit fake safety)\n84\t→ **接受率估算**: 1 task/2 model ~40% / 2 tasks+3 models ~55-65% / 3+ tasks ~65-75%\n85\t\n86\t### R2: Novelty of EE-only limitation\n87\t→ **应对**: 定量分析 (arm-body vs EE 碰撞比例 + oracle 排除其他解释); supporting claim 而非 primary\n88\t\n89\t### R3: No solution\n90\t\"诊断了问题但没解决\"\n91\t→ **应对**: (1) dfCAR metric 是 positive 工具贡献; (2) 揭示 avoidance 来源（implicit demo signal, not geometric supervision）本身是 actionable insight; (3) diagnostic paper 有方法论价值——知道问题在哪比错误地以为解决了更重要\n92\t\n93\t### R4: Action collapse is trivial\n94\t→ **应对**: 原因可能 trivial，但 metric contamination 后果 non-trivial; 后续工作基于被污染 CAR 得出错误结论\n95\t\n96\t### R5 (更新 D025): SDF redundancy — why bother testing it?\n97\t\"SDF 无效不是早该预见的吗？\"\n98\t→ **应对**: (1) 先验地，SDF geometric supervision 是合理的 safety method（motion planning 领域广泛使用）; (2) negative result 的价值在于排除一条看似合理的路径; (3) 关键 insight 不是 \"SDF 失败\" 而是 \"avoidance 来自 demo imitation, not geometry\" — 这对未来 safety method 设计有指导意义\n99\t\n100\t### R6 (新 D025): Fine-tuning collapse — is this just catastrophic forgetting?\n101\t\"TSR 73%→6% 可能只是小数据 fine-tuning 的 catastrophic forgetting，不是 safety 相关的发现\"\n102\t→ **应对**: (1) 可能确实是 catastrophic forgetting，但这恰恰说明当前 VLA fine-tuning pipeline 不适合 safety adaptation; (2) LoRA fine-tuning 同时提升 CAR 和降低 TSR — 模型学到了\"保守行为\"而非\"安全行为\"; (3) 区分 conservative avoidance vs genuine safety awareness 是后续工作方向\n103\t\n104\t## Narrative Structure (5 Blocks)\n105\t\n106\t### Block 1: Fake Safety Revelation (Claim 1)\n107\t- **Evidence**: eval_a1_lora_object_v11_rerun (800 episodes)\n108\t- **Key finding**: CAR=91.5%, obstacle displacement < 0.1mm in 99.6% safe episodes, TSR=0%\n109\t- **Metric**: \"obstacle displacement < 0.1mm\" + \"TSR=0%\" 双证据 = action collapse = fake safety\n110\t- **Contribution**: displacement-filtered CAR\n111\t\n112\t### Block 2: Stronger Models ≠ Safer (Claim 2)\n113\t- **Evidence**: eval_pi05_safelibero_object_v11 + spatial_v11\n114\t- **Key finding**: Pi0.5 CAR=28%, real_safe via geometric path (not avoidance behavior)\n115\t- **Narrative**: Capability↑ → motion↑ → collision↑; apparent safety is either frozen (Pi0) or path geometry (Pi0.5)\n116\t\n117\t### Block 3: Oracle Upper Bound (Claim 3)\n118\t- **Evidence**: 3 oracle variants, all < baseline\n119\t- **Narrative**: Runtime gradient correction structurally fails — alpha schedule and representation don't help\n120\t- **Presentation**: Single unified table\n121\t\n122\t### Block 4: EE-only Boundary (Claim 3)\n123\t- **Evidence**: spatial task eval, arm-body collision analysis\n124\t- **Narrative**: EE-only SDF = structural scope limit\n125\t\n126\t### Block 5: Fine-tuning Attribution — Real Avoidance from Demonstrations, Not Geometry (Claim 4, D025)\n127\t- **Evidence**: LoRA-only 2 seeds + SDF 3 seeds × 2 lambdas, per-task comparison\n128\t- **Key finding**: LoRA-only CAR=55% ≥ SDF CAR=52%, both TSR≈6%, identical per-task patterns\n129\t- **Narrative**: Fine-tuning on collision-free demonstrations produces genuine collision avoidance (+29pp CAR, 0% fake safety). Explicit SDF geometric supervision adds nothing. The avoidance signal is implicit in the training data. But both conditions suffer catastrophic task performance collapse — the model learns conservative behavior, not safe behavior.\n130\t- **Sub-narrative**: lambda curve (if SDF is redundant at 0.005/0.01, is it redundant at 0.1 too?) + Phase 2 (does SDF leave any persistent effect?)\n131\t\n132\t### 叙事原则\n133\t1. 每个 block 是 **evidence for structural claims**\n134\t2. Block 间逻辑递进：metric 有缺陷 (B1) → 强模型也不安全 (B2) → runtime 修正失败 (B3) → scope 边界 (B4) → fine-tuning 产生真实避障但 SDF 冗余 (B5)\n135\t3. B5 是 diagnostic result + negative finding，展示\"避障可实现但来源不是几何感知\"\n136\t\n137\t## Figure Plan\n138\t\n139\t| ID | 内容 | 优先级 | 数据来源 | 状态 |\n140\t|----|------|--------|---------|------|\n141\t| Fig 1 | Fake vs real safety 概念图 (displacement 对比) | 重要 | 设计 | 待做 |\n142\t| Fig 2 | EE Displacement 分布 (A1-frozen vs Pi0.5+A1-moving vs baseline) | **必须** | 修复后 eval JSON | 数据就绪 |\n143\t| Fig 3 | TSR-CAR scatter (多模型 + SDF tradeoff 线) | 重要 | 全部 eval 数据 | 数据就绪 |\n144\t| Fig 4 | Oracle refinement CAR bar chart | **必须** | 3 oracle + baselines | 数据就绪 |\n145\t| Table 1 | 3-seed × 2-lambda × best/30K 完整结果矩阵 + EE disp | **必须** | Pi0.5+A1 修正数据 | 数据就绪 |\n146\t| Fig 5 | Lambda-CAR/TSR 曲线 (含 LoRA baseline 作 λ=0 点) | **必须** | LoRA baseline + SDF 数据 | 待 LoRA 完成 |\n147\t| Table 2 | Phase 2 λ=0 ablation 结果 | 重要 | Phase 2 训练 | RUNNING |\n148\t\n149\t## Dependencies (Research Phase)\n150\t\n151\t- [x] Pi0.5+A1 3-seed × 2-lambda 训练 + eval — confirmed real avoidance (D023)\n152\t- [x] EE displacement 修正 eval — 3 seeds corrected, all consistent\n153\t- [x] A1 fake safety 800ep (Claim 1) — 99.6% fake (obstacle disp)\n154\t- [x] Oracle 3 variants (Claim 3) — all < baseline\n155\t- [x] Spatial/object collision analysis (Claim 3) — arm-body dominant\n156\t- [x] Pi0.5 baseline 3-seed (Claim 2) — CAR=26.8±1.6%\n157\t- [x] **LoRA baseline** (Claim 4 attribution) — DONE: CAR=55%, SDF delta=0pp → SDF redundant (D025)\n158\t- [ ] **LoRA baseline seed2** (plan_013) — 统计确认, RUNNING on westd-45947\n159\t- [ ] **Phase 2 λ=0** — RUNNING on cuda:3, 解读已调整(D025)\n160\t- [ ] **OpenVLA zero-shot eval** — BLOCKED (模型下载损坏)\n161\t- [ ] **spatial_bowl A1 训练** — RUNNING on cuda:0, ~20h\n162\t- [ ] **Lambda=0.1 × 2 seeds** — RUNNING on cuda:1-2, ~20h\n163\t- [ ] **Pi0.5 baseline re-eval** — 启动中 westd-45947, 补 EE displacement baseline 数据\n164\t- [ ] **Claim 1 EE disp re-eval** (术语验证) — 启动中 GPU 1, ~45min\n165\t- [ ] Lambda=0.1 bracket (4-point curve) — 待 GPU 释放\n166\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9cde0a5a-1128-4a6c-a947-5ccf4299c2ba","uuid":"f5c5ee68-c11f-416a-bbba-4e4fcefd3fcf","timestamp":"2026-05-26T03:13:41.190Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515/projects/diff_collision_sdf/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260526T023936/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# ColliForce-VLA Paper Framing\n\n> 维护者: Director | 最后更新: 2026-05-26 UTC | D023 修正：30K collapse 叙事被推翻，SDF 效果跨步数一致 | Post-MVP research phase\n\n## Core Insight\n\nVLA safety 评估存在系统性缺陷：collision avoidance rate (CAR) 被 action collapse 和几何路径安全严重污染，导致 \"安全\" 指标虚高。我们通过大规模实证分析（70+ 实验, 6000+ episodes）揭示这一系统性缺陷，提出 EE displacement-filtered CAR 作为修正指标，并证明 SDF auxiliary loss 能产生真实碰撞避免——但代价极端。\n\n## Working Title\n\n\"Rethinking VLA Safety Evaluation: When 98% of Collision Avoidance is an Illusion\"\n\n> 聚焦评估方法论贡献（影响面广、scope-proof），SDF 作为验证工具而非主贡献\n\n## Target Venue\n\n**Primary**: CoRL 2026 Main / ICRA 2027 (用户明确要求主会)\n**定位**: Diagnostic/evaluation methodology paper with positive method contribution\n**Fit**: Robotics safety track — \"VLA safety metrics are fundamentally broken\" 对社区有直接影响\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### Claim 1: Fake Safety (Primary — 证据强度 ★★★★★)\nStandard CAR metric is systematically contaminated. On SafeLIBERO, A1 (SDF auxiliary loss on Pi0) achieves 91.5% CAR, but 99.6% of safe episodes show obstacle displacement < 0.1mm — the robot is frozen, not collision-avoiding. \"Collision-free\" ≠ \"collision-avoiding.\"\n\n**证据**: 800 episodes A1 per-episode analysis (obstacle displacement ~5nm median); TSR=0% 独立确认 action collapse; Pi0.5 baseline 56/56 safe episodes = geometric path safety (非 avoidance 行为)\n**贡献**: 提出 EE displacement-filtered CAR (dfCAR) 作为修正指标\n**术语修正 (D023)**: 论文中 fake safety 判定以 TSR=0% + obstacle displacement < 0.1mm 双证据链为主，明确区分 \"obstacle displacement\" 和 \"EE displacement\"\n\n**dfCAR 定位 (D024 Dream 反馈)**:\n- Claim 1 的核心证据是 TSR=0% + obstacle displacement 双证据链，**不依赖** dfCAR\n- dfCAR 是 **方法论贡献**（community tool），不是 Claim 1 的唯一支撑\n- 论文需要展示 dfCAR 的实际 filtering 效果：Pi0+A1 (CAR=91.5% → dfCAR≈0%) vs Pi0.5+SDF (dfCAR=raw_CAR, no filtering)\n- Threshold sensitivity: δ∈[2mm, 200mm] 范围内 dfCAR 完全不变（所有 active episode 最小 EE disp = 239mm）\n- 待确认：800ep Pi0+A1 eval 数据是否可 post-hoc 提取 EE displacement\n\n### Claim 2: Task Capability vs Safety Anti-correlation (Secondary — 证据强度 ★★★)\n更强的 base model 完成更多任务但碰撞更多。Pi0.5 (TSR=74.7%) vs Pi0 (TSR≈0%): 能力越强 → 运动越多 → 碰撞越多。\n\n**证据**: Pi0.5 3-seed eval (TSR=74.7±1.5%, CAR=26.8±1.6%) vs Pi0 baseline (TSR≈0%, CAR=82%)\n**限制**: 仅 2 model families; Pi0 的 \"高 CAR\" 来自 action collapse; 降级为 observation, 不 claim 因果\n\n### Claim 3: EE-only SDF Structural Limitation (Supporting — 证据强度 ★★★★)\nEnd-effector-only SDF 在 action space 的碰撞避免存在结构性缺陷：SDF gradient 推 EE 远离障碍物但导致 arm body 扫过障碍物。\n\n**证据**: 3 组 GT SDF oracle (adaptive alpha, fixed alpha, feature-space) 均劣于 baseline; spatial vs object 碰撞部位分析; obstacle 高度/体积与碰撞率的单调关系\n**限制**: \"EE-only 不够\" 是 expected result; 缺乏 full-body SDF 对照\n\n### Claim 4: Fine-tuning Produces Real Avoidance; SDF is Redundant (Negative Finding — 证据强度 ★★★★) [D025]\nLoRA fine-tuning on collision-free SafeLIBERO demonstrations produces genuine collision avoidance (+29pp CAR, EE displacement ~0.48m, 0% fake safety) WITHOUT explicit geometric supervision. Adding SDF auxiliary loss contributes 0pp additional CAR — geometric supervision is redundant when demonstrations already encode avoidance behavior. Both LoRA-only and LoRA+SDF suffer identical catastrophic task performance collapse (TSR 73%→6%).\n\n**证据 (confirmed, D025)**:\n- LoRA-only (2 seeds): CAR=55.3%, TSR=6.3%, EE disp=0.478m, frozen=0%\n- LoRA+SDF λ=0.005 (3 seeds): CAR=50.5%, TSR=6.8%\n- LoRA+SDF λ=0.01 (3 seeds): CAR=52.8%, TSR=6.8%\n- Per-task CAR pattern 完全一致——高/低 CAR 由任务布局决定，非 SDF loss\n- SDF delta = -3pp (不显著, 在 ±3.5pp SE 内)\n\n**Claim 措辞**: \"LoRA fine-tuning on collision-free demonstrations produces genuine collision avoidance (+29pp CAR, 0% fake safety) on Pi0.5. Explicit SDF geometric supervision adds no additional benefit — the avoidance signal is already implicit in the training data. Both conditions suffer equal catastrophic task performance collapse (TSR: 73%→6%), indicating the tradeoff is a property of fine-tuning, not geometric supervision.\"\n\n**论文价值**: 这是一个有价值的 negative finding——揭示 VLA collision avoidance 的来源是训练数据中的隐式安全信号，而非显式几何感知。这对\"safety-by-design\"方法论有重要启示。\n\n**禁区**: SDF works / SDF contributes / geometric supervision helps\n\n**待确认**:\n- LoRA seed2 (plan_013) → 3v3 seeds 统计确认\n- Phase 2 λ=0 → 如果 SDF 无效，\"removing SDF\" 的实验解读需调整\n- Lambda=0.1 → 更强 SDF penalty 是否改变结论？\n\n### Phase 2 重新解读 (D025 后)\n\nPhase 2 (λ=0 resume from 10K SDF checkpoint) 的意义已改变：\n- 原意图：测试 SDF safety encoding 是否 persist → 如果 SDF 本身无效，persist 什么？\n- 新解读：Phase 2 测试的是\"10K 步 SDF 训练是否改变了模型行为相对于 LoRA-only\"\n- 如果 Phase 2 CAR ≈ LoRA-only (55%) → 进一步确认 SDF 无效（模型回归 LoRA-only 水平）\n- 如果 Phase 2 CAR < LoRA-only → SDF 训练可能造成持久损伤\n- 如果 Phase 2 CAR > LoRA-only → SDF 可能有微妙的持久效应（需要更多证据）\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### R1 (最致命): Generalizability\n\"仅在 SafeLIBERO + Pi0 系列上验证, 凭什么说 fake safety 是普遍问题?\"\n→ **应对**: (1) 2+ tasks (object_pudding + spatial_bowl); (2) 3+ models (Pi0 + Pi0.5 + OpenVLA); (3) 收窄 claim scope + mechanistic argument (any model with low task capability will exhibit fake safety)\n→ **接受率估算**: 1 task/2 model ~40% / 2 tasks+3 models ~55-65% / 3+ tasks ~65-75%\n\n### R2: Novelty of EE-only limitation\n→ **应对**: 定量分析 (arm-body vs EE 碰撞比例 + oracle 排除其他解释); supporting claim 而非 primary\n\n### R3: No solution\n\"诊断了问题但没解决\"\n→ **应对**: (1) dfCAR metric 是 positive 工具贡献; (2) 揭示 avoidance 来源（implicit demo signal, not geometric supervision）本身是 actionable insight; (3) diagnostic paper 有方法论价值——知道问题在哪比错误地以为解决了更重要\n\n### R4: Action collapse is trivial\n→ **应对**: 原因可能 trivial，但 metric contamination 后果 non-trivial; 后续工作基于被污染 CAR 得出错误结论\n\n### R5 (更新 D025): SDF redundancy — why bother testing it?\n\"SDF 无效不是早该预见的吗？\"\n→ **应对**: (1) 先验地，SDF geometric supervision 是合理的 safety method（motion planning 领域广泛使用）; (2) negative result 的价值在于排除一条看似合理的路径; (3) 关键 insight 不是 \"SDF 失败\" 而是 \"avoidance 来自 demo imitation, not geometry\" — 这对未来 safety method 设计有指导意义\n\n### R6 (新 D025): Fine-tuning collapse — is this just catastrophic forgetting?\n\"TSR 73%→6% 可能只是小数据 fine-tuning 的 catastrophic forgetting，不是 safety 相关的发现\"\n→ **应对**: (1) 可能确实是 catastrophic forgetting，但这恰恰说明当前 VLA fine-tuning pipeline 不适合 safety adaptation; (2) LoRA fine-tuning 同时提升 CAR 和降低 TSR — 模型学到了\"保守行为\"而非\"安全行为\"; (3) 区分 conservative avoidance vs genuine safety awareness 是后续工作方向\n\n## Narrative Structure (5 Blocks)\n\n### Block 1: Fake Safety Revelation (Claim 1)\n- **Evidence**: eval_a1_lora_object_v11_rerun (800 episodes)\n- **Key finding**: CAR=91.5%, obstacle displacement < 0.1mm in 99.6% safe episodes, TSR=0%\n- **Metric**: \"obstacle displacement < 0.1mm\" + \"TSR=0%\" 双证据 = action collapse = fake safety\n- **Contribution**: displacement-filtered CAR\n\n### Block 2: Stronger Models ≠ Safer (Claim 2)\n- **Evidence**: eval_pi05_safelibero_object_v11 + spatial_v11\n- **Key finding**: Pi0.5 CAR=28%, real_safe via geometric path (not avoidance behavior)\n- **Narrative**: Capability↑ → motion↑ → collision↑; apparent safety is either frozen (Pi0) or path geometry (Pi0.5)\n\n### Block 3: Oracle Upper Bound (Claim 3)\n- **Evidence**: 3 oracle variants, all < baseline\n- **Narrative**: Runtime gradient correction structurally fails — alpha schedule and representation don't help\n- **Presentation**: Single unified table\n\n### Block 4: EE-only Boundary (Claim 3)\n- **Evidence**: spatial task eval, arm-body collision analysis\n- **Narrative**: EE-only SDF = structural scope limit\n\n### Block 5: Fine-tuning Attribution — Real Avoidance from Demonstrations, Not Geometry (Claim 4, D025)\n- **Evidence**: LoRA-only 2 seeds + SDF 3 seeds × 2 lambdas, per-task comparison\n- **Key finding**: LoRA-only CAR=55% ≥ SDF CAR=52%, both TSR≈6%, identical per-task patterns\n- **Narrative**: Fine-tuning on collision-free demonstrations produces genuine collision avoidance (+29pp CAR, 0% fake safety). Explicit SDF geometric supervision adds nothing. The avoidance signal is implicit in the training data. But both conditions suffer catastrophic task performance collapse — the model learns conservative behavior, not safe behavior.\n- **Sub-narrative**: lambda curve (if SDF is redundant at 0.005/0.01, is it redundant at 0.1 too?) + Phase 2 (does SDF leave any persistent effect?)\n\n### 叙事原则\n1. 每个 block 是 **evidence for structural claims**\n2. Block 间逻辑递进：metric 有缺陷 (B1) → 强模型也不安全 (B2) → runtime 修正失败 (B3) → scope 边界 (B4) → fine-tuning 产生真实避障但 SDF 冗余 (B5)\n3. B5 是 diagnostic result + negative finding，展示\"避障可实现但来源不是几何感知\"\n\n## Figure Plan\n\n| ID | 内容 | 优先级 | 数据来源 | 状态 |\n|----|------|--------|---------|------|\n| Fig 1 | Fake vs real safety 概念图 (displacement 对比) | 重要 | 设计 | 待做 |\n| Fig 2 | EE Displacement 分布 (A1-frozen vs Pi0.5+A1-moving vs baseline) | **必须** | 修复后 eval JSON | 数据就绪 |\n| Fig 3 | TSR-CAR scatter (多模型 + SDF tradeoff 线) | 重要 | 全部 eval 数据 | 数据就绪 |\n| Fig 4 | Oracle refinement CAR bar chart | **必须** | 3 oracle + baselines | 数据就绪 |\n| Table 1 | 3-seed × 2-lambda × best/30K 完整结果矩阵 + EE disp | **必须** | Pi0.5+A1 修正数据 | 数据就绪 |\n| Fig 5 | Lambda-CAR/TSR 曲线 (含 LoRA baseline 作 λ=0 点) | **必须** | LoRA baseline + SDF 数据 | 待 LoRA 完成 |\n| Table 2 | Phase 2 λ=0 ablation 结果 | 重要 | Phase 2 训练 | RUNNING |\n\n## Dependencies (Research Phase)\n\n- [x] Pi0.5+A1 3-seed × 2-lambda 训练 + eval — confirmed real avoidance (D023)\n- [x] EE displacement 修正 eval — 3 seeds corrected, all consistent\n- [x] A1 fake safety 800ep (Claim 1) — 99.6% fake (obstacle disp)\n- [x] Oracle 3 variants (Claim 3) — all < baseline\n- [x] Spatial/object collision analysis (Claim 3) — arm-body dominant\n- [x] Pi0.5 baseline 3-seed (Claim 2) — CAR=26.8±1.6%\n- [x] **LoRA baseline** (Claim 4 attribution) — DONE: CAR=55%, SDF delta=0pp → SDF redundant (D025)\n- [ ] **LoRA baseline seed2** (plan_013) — 统计确认, RUNNING on westd-45947\n- [ ] **Phase 2 λ=0** — RUNNING on cuda:3, 解读已调整(D025)\n- [ ] **OpenVLA zero-shot eval** — BLOCKED (模型下载损坏)\n- [ ] **spatial_bowl A1 训练** — RUNNING on cuda:0, ~20h\n- [ ] **Lambda=0.1 × 2 seeds** — RUNNING on cuda:1-2, ~20h\n- [ ] **Pi0.5 baseline re-eval** — 启动中 westd-45947, 补 EE displacement baseline 数据\n- [ ] **Claim 1 EE disp re-eval** (术语验证) — 启动中 GPU 1, ~45min\n- [ ] Lambda=0.1 bracket (4-point curve) — 待 GPU 释放\n","numLines":166,"startLine":1,"totalLines":166}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BGEy9eFKchVCKWyiPrq4wT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the data. Let me synthesize the key information:\n\n**Experiment Data Summary:**\n\n1. **Claim 1 A1 EE displacement re-eval**: TSR=0%, CAR=91%, EE Disp safe=0.005mm, collision=45mm, Fake Safe=99.4%\n2. **OpenVLA zero-shot**: BLOCKED, projected TSR=0%, CAR=88%, Fake Safe=99%\n3. **LoRA baseline (2 seeds)**: s0 TSR=8.5%/CAR=54.5%, s1 TSR=4%/CAR=56%, mean TSR=6.25%/CAR=55.25%\n\n\n4. **LoRA baseline training**: Converged successfully\n5. **Phase 2 lambda=0 ablation**: Training complete with loss=0.0098, yielding TSR=42%, CAR=68%, EE displacement=0.42m\n6. **Spatial bowl variant**: Training done, eval shows TSR=3%, CAR=45%, EE displacement=0.35m\n7. **Lambda=0.1 experiments (2 seeds)**: Training finished, with s0 showing CAR=68\n\n%/TSR=2% and s1 at CAR=66%/TSR=3%, averaging CAR=67%/TSR=2.5%\n8. **Additional validation**: 50 epochs appears sufficient for Claim 1; seed0 adds TSR=38%, CAR=64%, EE displacement=0.44m; LoRA baseline across 3 seeds averages CAR=51.5% with 6.5pp standard deviation; threshold sensitivity analysis shows the metric is extremely robust; spatial bowl LoRA-only control achieves TSR=1%, CAR=36%\n9. **Paper direction**: The core argument is that VLA safety evaluation is fundamentally flawed and produces misleading results, with the strongest claim being that safety measures are fake, while secondary claims explore the relationship between task capability and other factors.\n10. **Narrative refinement**: The initial conclusion that SDF is redundant gets overturned when examining higher lambda values—at lambda=0.1, SDF actually contributes an additional 5-12pp CAR improvement; the low performance of LoRA seed2 (40-48% CAR) drags down the 3-seed average to around 50%; the two-phase strategy shows promise with CAR reaching 65-75% and TSR between 30-55%; spatial bowl and object pudding show inconsistent patterns, suggesting I should reframe away from \"SDF is redundant\" toward a decomposition perspective or two-phase discovery narrative; Claims 1-3 remain solid while Claim 4 becomes a more nuanced finding about fine-tuning producing real avoidance with SDF playing a complex role.\n\nNow I'm planning the full paper structure: Abstract, Introduction, Related Work, then Methods covering the SafeLIBERO benchmark, dfCAR metric, SDF auxiliary loss, and two-phase training approach. The Experiments section will map each finding to its corresponding analysis—fake safety diagnosis, dfCAR threshold sensitivity, model capability versus safety tradeoffs, LoRA fine-tuning attribution, lambda dose-response curves, the two-phase strategy validation, and cross-scene generalization. I need to ensure every experiment from the data has a corresponding section or table in the paper. Now I'm shifting to writing the full paper in CoRL 2026 format. The key narrative reframing is that SDF isn't redundant—at low lambda values the effect is too subtle to measure, but at lambda=0.1 there's a clear dose-response pattern with a +15.5pp CAR improvement. The two-phase training approach shows promise with 66% CAR and 40% TSR, though the spatial generalization results are inconsistent across scenes so I won't claim cross-scene transfer. I'm structuring this as: abstract, introduction covering VLA safety evaluation gaps and the dfCAR metric, related work, then building out the methodology and results sections. I'm deciding on the document format—CoRL would be the standard choice, but I'll go with a clean article template that prioritizes readability for review. Let me start writing the paper now.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17059,"cache_read_input_tokens":23228,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17059},"output_tokens":8,"se